Subject: [PATCH 08119/11362] [outer-loop] Diagnose ARC frontier exhaustion:
 g50t stop is a real bug, not exhaustion

The inert-label-defer A/B recorded g50t stopping at 1022 of 2000 actions with
timed_out=false, the run's largest "action saving" (-978), scored as a win.

It is not a saving. At the moment explored_out fired, all 56 nodes had zero
untested rows -- but 19 reachable untested (state, action) pairs leading to 7
never-observed states remained, counted directly by replaying the agent's own
recorded paths one ply.

Mechanism: untested rows are debited from the node the search INTENDS to probe,
while the probe executes wherever navigation actually landed. On g50t 118 of 141
navigate-probes fired from a different state, so 13 of 56 nodes were declared
exhausted having never been probed at all, and only 162 of 280 rows (58%)
executed where they were debited.

Not implicated: the REQ-ARC-WMTE-5836 global tier barrier never activates on
this nav-only game (no ACTION6, so tier_click_vocab_only never latches), and the
online discriminator pruned 0 nodes.

Root cause: the graph key is not a Markov state. 90 of 783 raw (state, action)
keys produced multiple successors under proven trajectory determinism, which
writes false forward edges and fabricated node paths.

Scope, stated honestly: the COLLAPSE is g50t-only (3 of 75 defer cells, 0 of 150
control cells) and is not extrapolated. The mis-attribution MECHANISM is
roster-wide -- median miss rate 10%, q3 63%, max 100% (tn36) -- severe in 8 of
25 games.

Adds a diagnostic probe only; changes no shipped default. CPU only, offline
arcade, no generator, no GPU, no scored game.

